            <div xml:id="d496">

                <pb facs="0474" n="462" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg462"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363/10–3044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-30T17:00:00+03:25">October 30, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 30—1:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>795. Following is exact text of my note to Prime Minister as requested in
                    Department’s 643, October 28:<anchor n="74" xml:id="d496-f1"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I have the honor to inform Your Excellency that I have been instructed
                            by my Government to inform Your Excellency’s Government that the
                            American Government has taken note of the Imperial Iranian Government’s
                            decision to postpone all negotiations in connection with petroleum
                            development in Iran. While the two American firms which have gone to
                            considerable expense and effort during the past year in pursuing these
                            negotiations are naturally disappointed my Government is confident that
                            the Iranian authorities were acting in good faith. The American
                            Government expects of course that if and when the Imperial Iranian
                            Government is in a position to consider applications for concessions the
                            applications which American nationals may wish to make will receive no
                            less favorable treatment than the applications made by the nationals or
                            Government of any other country. The American Government furthermore
                            expects that the Imperial Iranian Government will inform it or the
                            interested American companies immediately the Imperial Government is
                            ready to consider applications.</p>
                        <p>Accept Your Excellency the renewed assurances of my highest
                            consideration.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
